+   - Identify the 12 vertices of a regular icosahedron inscribed in the unit sphere.
+   - Identify the 20 vertices of a regular dodecahedron inscribed in the unit sphere.
+   - Combine these sets to form a pool of 32 unique vertices. Note that the icosahedron and dodecahedron are duals; their vertices correspond to the faces and vertices of each other, respectively.
