+3. **Recursive Subdivision:**
+   - For each level of refinement from $1$ to $k$:
+     - For each triangle in the current set of triangles:
+       - Calculate the midpoints of the three edges connecting the triangle's vertices.
+       - Normalize these midpoint vectors to lie on the unit sphere.
+       - Partition the original triangle into four new triangles by connecting the three normalized midpoints to each other and to the original vertices.
+       - Replace the original triangle with these four new triangles.
+   - After $k$ levels, the set of all triangle vertices constitutes the final quantized gradient directions.
 
